== A. retraction.  Experience x = 'told once that u -> v'.  Then u occurs five times and v does not follow
      (sensed).  Then x is retracted. ==
   design, life with x, before retraction                     W+ = 0.300  W- = 1.944  f = 0.134  c = 0.692  e = 0.247
   design, after subtracting the logged increments of x       W+ = 0.000  W- = 1.944  f = 0.000  c = 0.660  e = 0.170
   design, the life in which x never happened                 W+ = 0.000  W- = 0.000  f =   nan  c = 0.000  e = 0.500
      (in that life the tie u -> v does not even exist: exists = False)
   -> what is left after 'exact' retraction is 1.94 units of sensed evidence AGAINST a relation the mind would
      never have considered: c = 0.66 that u -> v is false (e = 0.17).  The five negative increments were
      weighted by an expectation that x had created; they are logged under the five later moments, not under x.
      The same holds for everything x changed downstream: trust-tie increments of the teller, chunk and
      recruitment decisions (thresholds on e), caps, and every inferred/imagined deposit computed while x was in.
   corrected (raw counts n+ per source on the tie; opportunities N on the unit u, per reporting channel):
      with x:      told W+ = 0.300; closed sense: 0 of 5 -> W- = 5.0;  f = 0.057, c = 0.841, e = 0.127
      x retracted: n+_told = 0;        closed sense: 0 of 5 -> W- = 5.0;  f = 0.000, c = 0.833, e = 0.083
      never told:  identical numbers (the five opportunities are a property of u's own history, counted whether
      or not a tie to v exists; a question 'u -> v?' reads n+ = 0 and N = 5 in both lives).

== B. float64.  1000 increments g*a_u (random in (0,1]) are added to one slot in life order; then 999 of them are
      retracted in a different order.  Residual error against the one increment that remains: ==
   exact in 0.0% of 2000 trials; max |error| = 1.77e-12; after retracting everything the slot is
   NEGATIVE in 50.7% of trials (violates w >= 0; f = W+/W then has the wrong sign or divides by ~0).
   'Exact' needs integer (fixed-point) counts or recomputation from the log, not float subtraction.

== C. W = 0.  A tie with no trust-weighted evidence (after retraction of its only experience; a PART or ABSTRACT
      tie at creation; a candidate tie created while the plasticity knob g = 0). ==
   literal §1:  f = 0/0 = nan,  c = 0,  e = c*(f - 1/2) + 1/2 = nan    (0 * nan = nan in IEEE 754)
   same quantity written as (W+ + k/2)/(W + k):  e = 0.5
   kWTA on activations [0.2, 0.9, nan, 0.4]: np.argmax -> index 2;  torch.topk(k=2) -> indices [2, 1], values [nan, 0.9]
   -> one evidence-free tie puts a NaN into settling and the NaN unit takes the focus.

== D. conflicting provenance.  While idle the mind IMAGINES u (u never occurred).  In the next moment the real
      event v arrives (sensed).  §2.5: 'v occurred: w+[pi] += g*a_u (pi = provenance of the confirming event)'. ==
   times this coincidence happened   w+[sensed](u -> v)   c       e(u -> v)
              1                           1.0          0.500    0.750
              3                           3.0          0.750    0.875
              5                           5.0          0.833    0.917
             20                          20.0          0.952    0.976
   -> the tie is booked as SENSED evidence that u is followed by v, at full trust, though u was never sensed.
      The same happens for a category unit (active only through ABSTRACT) and for an antecedent that settling
      ignited.  A tie increment has two ends; it is as real as the less real of them.

== E. lag-0 ties ('holds together'): the weight g*a_u is the SETTLED activation of u, and settling lets v raise u
      (the reverse tie v -> u).  If a_u = a+ in moments where v is present and a- where it is absent, even with
      unweighted negatives the frequency converges to  p a+ / (p a+ + (1-p) a-): ==
   true p   a+    a-     f the mind reads
    0.50    1.00  0.50      0.667
    0.30    1.00  0.50      0.462
    0.50    1.00  0.25      0.800
    0.20    1.00  0.25      0.500
   -> belief -> activation -> size of the evidence increment -> belief.  The evidence weight of an end must be
      its event-driven presence, not its settled activation.
